are  going to support the upcoming smart  connector keyboard cases with built in  track pads for the new cursor support  that works incredibly well and basically  helps make an iPad a pretty decent  laptop replacement the 10.2 inch iPad in  iPad air 3 get the Logitech combo touch  which is priced at 150 dollars but the  iPad pro actually gets the new magic  keyboard case which costs $300 but has a  number of advantages it features a USB C  port with pass-through charging meaning  that the main port is essentially freed  up for things like connecting storage  drives and other devices it's also the  first keyboard case that actually floats  the iPad and the air closer to you  making it more convenient touch while  also providing the same great magic key  switches that came with the 16 inch  macbook pro now with all of that said  and compared let's get into my  purchasing recommendations for which  ipad you should buy starting with who  should buy the 10.2 inch budget iPad and  why if you're buying an iPad for a child  you should probably go with the budget  iPad it's going to be good enough for  them to listen to music watch Netflix  and play basic games  chances are they  won't really mind the lower performance  or the worst quality display and if they  drop it and crack the screen it's  cheaper to replace since it's non  laminated and for adults it's by far the  cheapest way to get an iPad with a  trackpad keyboard case this is great for  someone who needs a cheaper laptop  replacement for doing things like  browsing the web using common apps like  QuickBooks and typing documents and  other business-related tasks now if  you're buying an iPad for a teenager  chances are they'll appreciate the extra  performance of the a12 chip and both the  iPad Mini and the iPad air as they'll  perform much better for gaming these  iPads are also great for those who  really care about display quality for  things like watching Netflix and  especially for those who want to use  their Apple pencil to draw with their  iPad I'd say the Mini is more for those  who would rather save $100 instead of  having the ability to use it with a  keyboard case and of course those who  don't mind the smaller display size now  the air is for people who want a premium  iPad that works as a laptop replacement  and has extra power to make sure all of  those apps work quickly and very  reliably especially while multitasking  the only limitation is the lightning  port which makes it difficult to connect  storage devices for file transfers and  that's where the iPad pro comes in with  its USB C port which is by far the best  case scenario for being a laptop  replacement the pro is for someone who  wants the absolute best iPad experience  you can get regardless of the price the  incredible performance the six gigs of  ram in the 120 Hertz display make it by  far the snappiest tablet out there  whether you're using it for gaming  drawing with the Apple pencil 2 or for  productivity work like video or photo  editing the pro is for those who are  initially considering an apple macbook  but would rather have the thin  lightweight and portable design of the  iPad pro instead it's got  top-of-the-line specs like Wi-Fi 6 it's  got the best cameras speakers and  microphones for those who care about  them and it's also the most future proof  by packing the new lidar scanner for  those who are interested in augmented  reality the choice you make really  depends on what you're going to be doing  with your iPad and in many cases paying  the extra price is worth it  because you don't want to be stuck with  a budget 10.2 inch iPad if you're trying  to play Fortnite competitively and on  the flip side you don't need to buy the  iPad pro if all you're going to be using  it for is watching Netflix and scrolling  through Facebook basically a good rule  of thumb is to choose the iPad you buy  wisely based on what you can expect to  do with it a year from today so  hopefully this video helps you make a  decision and if you've made up your mind  we'll have links to all of these iPads  down in the description below if you  enjoy this video tap like and click the  circle above to subscribe thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

